---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const sections = [['scope','Scope'],['data','Data we access'],['use','How data is used'],['sharing','Services & sharing'],['storage','Storage & retention'],['control','Your choices'],['contact','Contact']];
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy policy — Agoca Labs" description="How Agoca Labs accesses, processes, stores, and shares data for its Email Manager and video-publishing workflows.">
<div class="policy-header wrap"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY & DATA</p><h1>Your data.<br />A clear explanation.</h1><p class="policy-date">Privacy policy · Effective September 12, 2026</p><p>This policy describes the Agoca Labs website, the personal Email Manager automation, and the creator-operated English and Spanish video-publishing workflow.</p></div>
<div class="policy-layout wrap"><nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">{sections.map(([id,label])=><a href={'#'+id}>{label}</a>)}</nav><article class="policy-content">
<section id="scope"><h2>01. Who this policy covers</h2><p>Agoca Labs is an independent project operated by Agoca. Its automations and creator tools are currently used with accounts authorized by the operator. This website provides information about the project and does not collect Google or TikTok passwords.</p><p>This policy covers information accessed through connected Google and TikTok accounts, messages exchanged with the Telegram bot, creator-approved video assets, publication records, and technical information associated with visiting this website.</p></section>
<section id="data"><h2>02. Data we access</h2><ul><li><strong>Gmail:</strong> selected message content and metadata, including sender, subject, date, message identifiers, and read status, to classify email and prepare summaries.</li><li><strong>Google Sheets:</strong> classification rules and preferences in the connected rules spreadsheet. Confirmed rule updates are written back to that spreadsheet.</li><li><strong>Telegram:</strong> chat identifiers, messages, replies, approvals, and conversational context needed to respond to requests, update rules, and control creator workflows.</li><li><strong>TikTok profile information:</strong> basic information made available with authorization, such as an account identifier, display name, and avatar, so the workflow can identify the connected profile and route English and Spanish videos to the intended account.</li><li><strong>Video-publishing information:</strong> creator-approved video files, captions, language and account routing, publication status, TikTok content identifiers, timestamps, and error details needed to upload or publish and monitor the result.</li><li><strong>Connection information:</strong> OAuth access and refresh tokens needed to use authorized Google and TikTok services. Those services handle account sign-in; the automation does not need account passwords.</li><li><strong>Website requests:</strong> the hosting provider may process IP addresses, browser information, request timestamps, and security or diagnostic logs to deliver and protect the website.</li></ul></section>
<section id="use"><h2>03. What we do with it</h2><p>Email Manager analyzes selected email using locally hosted AI models, applies the configured rules, and prepares a brief highlighting important messages and useful updates. It sends that brief to the configured Telegram chat. Configured workflows may also mark processed Gmail messages as read.</p><p>Telegram conversations help interpret rule-change requests and record creator approvals. Confirmed updates are saved for later runs. Workflow execution records may contain input messages, model outputs, approval events, and error details used to operate and troubleshoot the automations.</p><p>For TikTok publishing, Agoca Labs uses authorized profile information to identify the intended English or Spanish account. Only a creator-approved final video and its associated caption are sent to TikTok. An approved English master may be sent to the English account; an approved Spanish master may be sent to the Spanish account after its separate review. Draft-upload capability may be used for testing or as a creator-controlled fallback.</p><p>Connected-service data is not sold, used for advertising, or used to train general-purpose AI models. Local model inference produces classifications, summaries, and creator assets; it does not train the underlying models.</p><p class="callout">Agoca Labs' use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p></section>
<section id="sharing"><h2>04. Where information goes</h2><p>Local AI processing does not mean every part of the workflow stays on one device. These services support the features described above:</p><ul><li><strong>Google</strong> stores the original Gmail messages and connected Google Sheets data and provides the authorized APIs.</li><li><strong>The operator's server</strong> runs n8n and local AI services to coordinate workflows, process content, and retain operational records.</li><li><strong>Telegram</strong> receives generated briefs, video previews, status messages, and approval actions, and processes bot conversations.</li><li><strong>TikTok</strong> receives approved video files, captions, authorization information, and publishing requests for the connected creator account.</li><li><strong>ngrok</strong> provides HTTPS endpoints for incoming messages, service callbacks, and access to the automation interface; traffic through those endpoints is processed by ngrok.</li><li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this public informational website and may process website request and security logs. The site itself does not display private inbox or connected-account data.</li></ul><p>Service providers handle information under their own applicable terms and privacy policies. Data is shared only as needed to deliver the configured features, comply with the creator's instructions, meet legal obligations, or address security incidents.</p></section>
<section id="storage"><h2>05. Storage, retention & security</h2><p>The automation stores configuration, connection tokens, creator approvals, publication identifiers, and workflow execution data on the operator's server. n8n encrypts saved credentials using its instance encryption key. This does not mean all workflow execution content or creator assets are encrypted at rest.</p><p>Retention depends on configured execution-history settings, operational needs, and manual cleanup. There is currently no single automatic deletion period across all connected services. Rules remain in Google Sheets until edited or removed; messages and approvals remain in Telegram according to its settings; final videos and publication records remain until deleted or no longer needed for the workflow.</p><p>Copies in backups, if backups are enabled, may remain until those backups are removed or expire. Revoking account access prevents future authorized access but does not automatically delete existing messages, videos, execution records, published TikTok posts, or backups.</p><p>Access controls, credential encryption, and HTTPS on public endpoints help protect information. No system can guarantee absolute security. Avoid including information in messages or media that is unnecessary for the automation.</p></section>
<section id="control"><h2>06. Your choices</h2><p>You can revoke Google access through your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google Account connections</a>. TikTok access can be revoked through the connected TikTok account's security or application settings. The operator can also disconnect credentials, stop workflows, delete execution history, and remove stored configuration or creator assets.</p><p>Revoking TikTok access stops new publishing through the authorization but does not remove videos already posted. Published posts and connected-service content must be managed in TikTok, Gmail, Google Sheets, or Telegram as applicable. For questions about access or removal of information held by the automation, contact the operator using the address below.</p><p>This website does not add advertising trackers, analytics scripts, or a contact form. Hosting and security services may still process technical request information.</p></section>
<section id="contact"><h2>07. Contact & policy updates</h2><p>For privacy questions or data-removal requests, email <a href="mailto:agomezcasarez@gmail.com">agomezcasarez@gmail.com</a>.</p><p>This policy will be updated when the project changes how it handles information. The effective date above identifies the current version. Material new uses of connected Google data will be disclosed, and additional consent will be requested where required.</p></section>
</article></div></SiteLayout>
